  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-41201463" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save the Children Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Work: No Child&apos;s Business - Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme will focus on children and adolescents subject to or at risk of child labour and their families. Especially children and youth in artisanal and small-scale mining and pastoralist communities will be main beneficiaries. Children between the ages of 13 and 15 will be an important focus of programme interventions related to child protection and skill building.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme will target all four Pathways of Change to reach the intended long-term vision of ensuring `Children and youth are free from child labour and enjoy their rights to quality education and (future) decent work, hereby contributing to SDG 8.7`. The programme will work on a comprehensive approach to tackle child labour in Karamoja and Busia, addressing both the current child labour practices as well as the root causes in order to prevent child labour.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Work: No Child&#xE2;&#x20AC;&#x2122;s Business&#xE2;&#x20AC;&#x2122; is a programme of an alliance consisting of the Stop Child Labour Coalition, UNICEF Netherlands and Save the Children that aims to make a strong and lasting contribution to the elimination of child labour in Uganda.</narrative>
  </description>
